1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
How could someone crush sales in 2022?

2
00:00:02,320 --> 00:00:03,980
My biggest advice to most salesmen

3
00:00:03,980 --> 00:00:05,790
is no one likes to be

4
00:00:05,790 --> 00:00:07,600
sold to, but everybody likes to buy.

5
00:00:07,900 --> 00:00:09,030
So what you do is you

6
00:00:09,030 --> 00:00:10,160
put something in front of them

7
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:12,200
and I call it solution selling.

8
00:00:12,320 --> 00:00:13,380
There's lots of names for it.

9
00:00:13,760 --> 00:00:15,480
I sell by asking questions,

10
00:00:15,740 --> 00:00:18,460
understanding first what the real true need is,

11
00:00:18,520 --> 00:00:19,880
and then see if I

12
00:00:19,880 --> 00:00:21,240
can help them solve that need.

13
00:00:21,540 --> 00:00:22,720
I don't come in and say,

14
00:00:22,860 --> 00:00:25,200
a lot of young salespeople come in and say,

15
00:00:25,580 --> 00:00:26,520
hey, let me do a demo.

16
00:00:26,680 --> 00:00:27,640
Let me show you everything I got.

17
00:00:27,720 --> 00:00:29,140
And when you see something, stop me.

18
00:00:29,140 --> 00:00:30,420
And that's just the wrong way to sell.

19
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:31,900
That's like throwing shit against the wall

20
00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:32,680
and seeing what sticks.

21
00:00:32,860 --> 00:00:34,640
What I'm saying is slow down,

22
00:00:34,760 --> 00:00:36,020
do a lot of homework on your client

23
00:00:36,020 --> 00:00:37,260
before you ever show up,

24
00:00:37,300 --> 00:00:38,240
because nobody does that,

25
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:40,060
understand their pain points,

26
00:00:40,120 --> 00:00:41,460
and make sure you're talking to them

27
00:00:41,460 --> 00:00:43,920
about those pain points and mutually solve a problem

28
00:00:43,920 --> 00:00:45,700
as opposed to trying to sell them

29
00:00:45,700 --> 00:00:46,960
something like off the back of a truck.

